Yes, 20 years....my first game was on a DEC in January of 1986. See the 
details under Nethack addiction at  
http://archive.gamespy.com/legacy/halloffame/nethack_b.shtm

Instead of the usual playing like a drunken fool hooked on the game, the 
adventures of Gravitoid the Tourist took 3 months. Sectioned out in 
mostly 2 hour increments for 2 months till I was ready for The Dash. The 
game stayed dormant for a month, Gravitoid quietly standing outside the 
entrace to Rodney's tower. Today, in two sections of 2 hours each, I 
finally saw the Planes and ascended!

The early game was usual Tourist saga of hit, run, backtrack, try a 
different branch (Mines, Sokoban,main dungeon) till I accumulated a 
decent weapon and some skill -- espcially with twoweaponing. Gravtoid 
ascended twoweaponing with Grayswandir and a crysknife. The Lady 
provided such wonderful gifts of Mjollinar, Demonbane, Giantslayer, 
Dranonbane, Cleaver, and Magicbane. They are all resting safely in a 
locked box on level 12.

This dungeon the RNG was kind enough to provide an altar almost every 3 
levels to the 20th. Minetown and the 20th level contained co-aligned 
priests. Not that a good sacfest provided anything of use. But, I was 
able to get a BUC status on everything easily.

Gravitoid used 10 wishes: the first from a magic lamp in Minetown 
yielded spellbooks of Identify (purchasing a spellbook of light and 
lighting up Minetown, I was skilled enough to ID all my kit). Another 
wish from a throne on the 17th level provided speed boots. The castle 
wand yielded SDSM, helm of brilliance, and a magic marker. 3 wishes were 
used on magic markers during the game; the RNG chose not to provide 
otherwise. 3 wishes for spellbooks: ID, charm monster, and magic 
mapping. 2 wishes for Gauntlets of dexterity -- Rodney decided to steal 
the first ones. One WoW was found on Orcus level. I ascended with 3 
wishes unused.

Ludios was one level below the altar with co-aligned priest; so 
covenient. Useful when I lost my protection when I had to kill another 
god's priest and use his altar for a sacfest.

I genocided the usual suspects: kraken, eels, mind flayers of all types, 
Lich and kenfolk.

Hell was....welll, Hell. Magic mapped out all the levels, dug my running 
lanes and RAN. Rodney and the priest of Moloch were kind enough to stand 
in line so one shot of the Wand of Death took out both of them. Since I 
was prepared, the Planes were not a problem. Earth was tedious, water 
was frustrating, and Charm Monster took care of Air. But, the Amulet 
sucked all my mojo -- major unplanned incident. Astral was tedious since 
I was without mojo and could not charm. The Four Riders each took two 
tries at me; Pestilence annoyed me greatly once. But a huge stock of 
wands and PYEC to renew a wand of death found the correct altar on the 
second room. I could not believe my own priest was trying to bash me to 
death while I was offering the Amulet. (probably petty jealousy)

Gravitoid the Tourist ascended with 3512526 points, 198 HP, no cash, no 
jewels, and only one artifact.
